@startuml runtime-03-chain-set
' Runtime scenario 3 - verify before write.
' Canonical source for docs/architecture/arc42.md section 6.3.
' evm chain set is the most elaborate write path in the CLI: a local edit that
' takes a network round trip in order to be correct. evm explorer set has the
' same shape with a key probe in place of the chain-id check.

title Runtime scenario 3 - verify before write (evm chain set)

actor Operator
participant "chain set handler" as H
participant "lib/chains" as Ch
participant "lib/profile-file" as PF
participant "lib/rpc" as Rpc
participant "RPC endpoint" as Node
database "profile YAML" as File

Operator -> H: evm chain set base https://base.example/rpc [-H name:value] [--no-verify --chain-id N]
activate H

H -> H: chain name matches the permitted pattern
H -> Ch: resolveProfileTarget(options.profile)
activate Ch
Ch --> H: name and path
deactivate Ch

alt profile file does not exist
  H -> Operator: "Profile not found", exit 1
  note left of H
    Only the default profile is created on
    demand. A -p naming anything else is a
    typo rather than a request for a new file.
    readProfileDocument would happily start an
    empty document, so the handler checks first.
  end note
end

H -> PF: readProfileDocument(path)
activate PF
PF -> File: read
File --> PF: text
PF --> H: YAML Document, comments and key order intact
deactivate PF
H -> PF: getChain(doc, chain)
activate PF
PF --> H: existing entry, or undefined
deactivate PF

alt --no-verify
  note right of H
    Requires --chain-id, because the check
    being skipped is the only source of
    that value. The escape hatch for a node
    that is not running yet.
  end note
  H -> H: chainId = the given --chain-id
else default: verify against the endpoint
  H -> Ch: buildEndpoint(rpcUrl, headers)
  activate Ch
  note right of Ch
    Environment references are resolved only
    to reach the endpoint, so an unverified
    entry can name variables absent from
    this shell.
  end note
  Ch --> H: endpoint, or a throw
  deactivate Ch
  H -> Rpc: createDetectingProvider(endpoint)
  activate Rpc
  Rpc --> H: provider with network detection on
  deactivate Rpc
  H -> Node: eth_chainId, raced against a 5 s timer
  activate Node
  Node --> H: chain id, or no response
  deactivate Node
  H -> H: provider.destroy() in finally

  alt no response, or the id contradicts --chain-id
    H -> Operator: reports what the endpoint said and that nothing was written, exit 1
  end
  H -> H: chainId = the id the endpoint reported
end

H -> Ch: loadBundledChains()
activate Ch
note right of Ch
  Matched on chain id, not on chain name,
  so a fork of a known chain inherits its
  symbol, coingecko_id and explorer_api.
  Best-effort: an unreadable bundle just
  means no suggestions.
end note
Ch --> H: bundled entries
deactivate Ch
H -> H: precedence per field:\nexplicit option, then existing entry, then bundled

H -> PF: setChain(doc, chain, edit)
activate PF
note right of PF
  An existing mapping is edited in place so
  its comments survive; anything else is
  replaced with a freshly built entry in the
  canonical field order.
end note
PF --> H: document mutated
deactivate PF
H -> PF: writeProfileDocument(path, doc)
activate PF
PF -> File: write to path.pid.tmp at mode 0600, then rename
note right of PF
  An interrupted edit cannot truncate a
  working profile. On failure the temp file
  is unlinked and the error propagates.
end note
File --> PF: ok
PF --> H: written
deactivate PF

H -> Operator: reports added or updated, and the fields now stored
deactivate H

@enduml
